I tried to experiment how to offload an existing SA session onto another dedicated Interface to understand how a network session is offloaded to a data plane path than to rely on a CPU core. 

modprobe netdevsim || { apt -y install linux-modules-extra-$(uname -r); modprobe netdevsim; }
echo "10 1" > /sys/bus/netdevsim/new_device
ip addr add 192.168.123.3/24 dev $DEV
ip link set $DEV up









"ethtool -k $DEV | grep esp"

The below output should be seen 

esp-hw-offload: on
esp-tx-csum-hw-offload: on

Indicating esp / hw offload is turned on. 

1. Initialise an SA connection
sudo ip xfrm state add proto esp src 192.168.123.3 dst 192.168.123.4 \

2. Specify the parameter for identifying an SA

  spi 0x100 reqid 42 mode transport replay-window 32 \

3. Encryption Config 

  aead 'rfc4106(gcm(aes))' 0x3132333435363738393031323334353664636261 128 \

4. Hand it off to the dummy NIC 

  sel src 192.168.123.3/32 dst 192.168.123.4/32 offload dev $DEV dir out